  clock: 2  # 22eb
  nonce: 22eb  # 22eb
  message: "MEASURED, AND IT CORRECTS BOTH THIS ITEM'S METHOD AND ITS SIZING. I filed both;\nboth were wrong in the same direction.\n\n*** METHOD: THIS ITEM PROPOSED THE CRITERION THE TARGET FILE EXPLICITLY FORBIDS. ***\nThe description above lists builtins to summarise BY CALL FREQUENCY (len 4660,\nstr 1826, ...). python_stdlib.yaml's own header states its scope rule:\n\"ENUMERATION-DERIVED, NOT A STDLIB SURVEY ... every entry is a callee the section\n3a walk was measured consulting at a real escape site\", and warns that\nspeculative entries \"would only make this file look more complete than it is\".\nFrequency is exactly that speculative criterion. Withdrawn.\n\n*** THE ENUMERATION-DERIVED ANSWER, via scripts/measure-call-escape-cause.py,\nwhich reads production's own _is_taint_call_edge / _catalogue_key_for_edge /\n_summary_terminates rather than reimplementing them. ***\nCorpus: packages/hypergumbo-core (532 .py), post-INV-foluz tree.\n\n  positive control\n    edges offered to _is_taint_call_edge   348,132\n    accepted as taint call edges           226,364\n    section 4 summary index entries             69\n    callees_at entries given to the walk    68,368\n    escape events captured                     124\n\n  CALL-node escape sites: 8\n    3a  no receiver type, 'external' placeholder (INV-linub)   3   37.5%\n    3b  resolved and provenance-gated (CORRECT, WI-zumud)      2   25.0%\n    4a  KEY PRESENT, NO SUMMARY  (this item's cohort)          2   25.0%\n    1   no edge emitted at all (INV-mumov)                     1   12.5%\n\n  THE COHORT, IN FULL. Two sites, two callees:\n    cli.py:11933   builtins.hasattr\n    cli.py:4086    builtins.float\n\n*** SO THE MECHANISM I DESCRIBED IS CONFIRMED AND ITS MAGNITUDE IS NOT. *** Both\nsites are INV-foluz's new edges: hasattr and float are bare builtin calls that\nemitted nothing before PR #711, so they took the \"no callee -> not an escape\"\nbranch. They now take \"callee with no terminating summary -> ESCAPE\". That is\nexactly the conversion this item was filed on. But it is TWO SITES, not the\nthousands my \"12,734 edges are not consultable\" framing implied. An edge only\ncosts a refutation when it lands at a line that (a) is on a tainted value's path\nand (b) has an heir; almost none do.\n\n*** WHAT THIS MEANS FOR WI-kabif, stated plainly because the owner's sequencing\nruling was made on my overestimate. *** The owner ruled WI-vosug before Phase D\non the strength of \"Phase A makes the substrate more conservative\". Direction:\nstill true. Size: 2 sites on this corpus, addressable by 2 YAML rows. That is a\nmuch weaker reason to gate Phase D than I gave, and the owner should get the\nchance to re-decide rather than inherit a blocker sized from a guess.\n\n*** CAVEAT CARRIED, NOT BURIED: ONE CORPUS. *** hypergumbo-core is our own code\nand its escape population is small. The pretix run was attempted first and the\ninstrument REFUSED THE TABLE -- no call-node vocabulary is declared for\njavascript (5 sites), so the counts would be an undercount of unknown size\n(WI-nukut). That refusal is the instrument working; it is also why this measures\none repository rather than two. pretix's python subtree carries 164 .js/.ts\nfiles, so it cannot be trivially isolated. A second corpus requires WI-nukut or a\ngenuinely pure-python repository, and the shape above should not be treated as\nsettled until one exists.\n\n*** RE-SCOPED DELIVERABLE. *** Add section 4 summaries for builtins.hasattr and\nbuiltins.float, each argued individually:\n  hasattr(obj, name) -> bool. Returns nothing derived from the argument's\n    CONTENT; terminating. Note it does leak EXISTENCE, which is not the same as\n    the value.\n  float(x) -> a numeric value DERIVED FROM x. Propagating (param_to_return),\n    NOT terminating -- a tainted numeric string that becomes a float is still\n    attacker-influenced.\nNote those two verdicts differ, which is the argument against bulk-stamping a\nfrequency list: half of it would have been wrong in the deleting direction, and\nsince PR #214 a wrong TERMINATING summary licenses a False, earns `sanitized`,\nand DROPS a flow."  # 22eb
